# What must NOT be excluded here is more important than what is.
#
# .git STAYS IN THE CONTEXT. cmake/revision.h.cmake shells out to git for the
# commit hash and falls back to "unknown 1970-01-01 (Archived)" when there is no
# repository -- silently, because that fallback exists for source tarballs. An
# `.git` line in this file is the easy way to ship an image that cannot say
# which commit built it, and nothing fails to warn you.
#
# The rest is the local build tree. A developer's build/ directory is the object
# tree -- around 20 GB with DEBUG_SYMBOLS on -- and without these lines every
# byte of it is tarred up and sent to the daemon before the first RUN, on a
# build that is going to discard it and compile from scratch anyway.
build/
build-*/
out/
stage/
.ccache/
configure.log

# Editor and OS noise. Harmless in the image, but each one is a context change
# that invalidates the COPY layer and every layer after it.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
